			],
			"Message": "chore(Output): Sync Output submodule to latest bundled artifacts\n\nUpdate the Output submodule (compiled JS bundles from Rest) from 1060f224 to de62ac1e.\n\nThe Output submodule contains bundled JavaScript artifacts consumed by Cocoon at runtime. This routine sync brings in the latest built artifacts from the Rest bundler.",
			"SHA": "c181cb1fb55f7a4654938b157c335c09bf249c64"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T23:39:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Wire Cocoon RPC handlers to trait implementations for state tracking\n\nCross-cutting submodule sync with Mountain refactor and Output cleanup:\n\n1. Mountain: Replace direct Sky event emissions with proper trait implementations across SCM, StatusBar, Webview, and Search handlers:\n   - SCM: RegisterScmProvider and UpdateScmGroup now use SourceControlManagementProvider trait to materialize state in ApplicationState::SourceControl\n   - StatusBar: CreateStatusBarItem and SetStatusBarText now use StatusBarProvider::SetStatusBarEntry to store entries in ActiveStatusBarItems\n   - Webview: CreateWebviewPanel and SetWebviewHtml now use WebviewProvider trait to register panels in ApplicationState::WebviewState\n   - Search: findFiles delegates to WorkspaceProvider::FindFilesInWorkspace; findTextInFiles delegates to SearchProvider::TextSearch\n\n2. Output: Remove Configuration directory (ESBuild, Plugin, Polyfill, Service configs and tsconfig files)\n\n3. Cocoon: Submodule sync to cbaf44f1\n\nImpact: SCM providers, status bar items, and webview panels now properly persist in Mountain's ApplicationState. File and text search now use ignore-aware glob walking and proper trait implementations.",
			"SHA": "5691989860608841ff65a2f7c25c102d27f039a1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T23:16:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Sync Mountain and Cocoon submodules\n\nMountain: Add regex and multiline search options to TextSearchQuery\n- Add `isRegExp` and `isMultiline` fields mirroring VS Code's ITextSearchQuery\n- Escape plain-text search patterns via regex::escape() to prevent crashes on metacharacters like `.`, `(`, `[`, `*`, `?`\n- Add .multi_line() support for multiline regex searches\n- Fixes Search view plain-text mode broken for queries containing `obj.method(` or `file[1].txt`\n\nCocoon: Updated to d4763554\n\nImpact: Plain-text search now works correctly for queries containing regex metacharacters without crashing the regex compiler.",
			"SHA": "ea16cc733978b6e27920c190adaa149e9f1c0475"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T23:05:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Wire search IPC handlers to trait implementations\n\nReplace naive inline fs-walk implementations in Search.rs with delegations to properly-implemented trait methods on MountainEnvironment:\n- `handle_search_find_in_files` → `SearchProvider::TextSearch` (grep-searcher + ignore::WalkBuilder with parallel walking)\n- `handle_search_find_files` → `WorkspaceProvider::FindFilesInWorkspace` (ignore-aware glob walker with .gitignore support)\n\nThe inline implementations had multiple deficiencies: naive `starts_with('.')` hidden-file skipping (doesn't honour .gitignore), no regex engine, bogus `format!(\"file://{}\")` URI constructor, and single-threaded walkers. The trait implementations were reachable only through `Environment.Require<dyn SearchProvider>()` calls and no IPC handler ever issued those.\n\nAlso change FileReaddirNative.rs log level from `vfs-verbose` to `vfs` since readdir fires at most once per folder expand (unlike stat which fires per probe) and is the primary observable for Explorer view diagnostics.\n\nImpact: File search and find-files now use proper ignore rules, parallel walking, and regex support instead of naive single-threaded implementations.",
			"SHA": "2478d6ec0535cc41ce3e2a38eba71a7a941f0658"
		}
	],
